00:09:08.240 --> 00:09:16.920
like, the output y of z. And so the surrogate&nbsp;
modeling problem from data is then to say, Okay,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.920 --> 00:09:24.480
let's suppose that f hat is a parameterized&nbsp;
model with parameters beta. And so I can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.480 --> 00:09:29.200
choose some parameters beta, and then I have some&nbsp;
input, and then I can give it my input variable,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.200 --> 00:09:35.520
Z, and it will predict outputs. So the machine&nbsp;
learning task is then to find the best parameters&nbsp;&nbsp;

